  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "name": "Multi-Organ Dysfunction and Failure",
      "description": "Critical illness often leads to dysfunction across multiple organ systems (renal, hepatic, cardiac, respiratory, neurological). Biomarkers such as creatinine (renal), bilirubin and AST (hepatic), and eGFR provide direct quantification of organ damage. Organ dysfunction worsens prognosis by disrupting homeostasis, reducing resilience to stressors, and limiting recovery potential.",
